dendum v0.4 Date: 2026-09-18 Status: APPEND-ONLY PHYSICAL-CALORIMETRY BRANCH REPAIR / SUPERSEDES v0.3 FOR PHYSICAL LANE Physical promotion: 0 A. Physical calorimetry branch For the phase-slip nanocalorimetry lane, freeze: OBSERVATION_BRANCH = ENERGY_SOURCE The source observable is event heat Qk. Q_k. The candidate native burden bridge is εk=Qk/EB. \\varepsilon_k=Q_k/E_B. B. Do not apply amplitude-variance subtraction Do not subtract βVar(wk) \\beta\\,\\operatorname{Var}(w_k) from physical heat unless a separately preregistered and independently sourced theorem establishes Q=β|w|2 Q=\\beta |w|^2 for the apparatus. Return empirical heat variance/covariance for uncertainty propagation. C. Frozen winding statistics Use source-isolated class heat means: RB=Q1/Q0, R_B=Q_1/Q_0, D2Q=Q2−2Q1+Q0. D_2^{Q}=Q_2-2Q_1+Q_0. Under a common energy-to-burden scale, κ=D2Q/Q0RB−1 \\boxed{ \\kappa = \\frac{ D_2^Q/Q_0 }{ R_B-1 } } for RB≠1R_B\\ne1. No numerical EBE_B is needed for this dimensionless ratio. D. Leakage/confounding The existing leakage/non-stationarity sidecar remains required. Heat covariance must not be silently set to zero. E. Absolute burden guard Do not report absolute dimensionless εk \\varepsilon_k without an independently anchored EBE_B. F. Optional constellation channel The linear constellation/curl readout remains optional as an orthogonal source/preparation diagnostic. It is not required to score the current frozen energy-source winding family. G. Future mean-amplitude branch Any future MEAN_AMPLITUDE_SOURCE proposal is a separate frontier object and must independently derive/calibrate the amplitude→heat map before use. Physical promotion remains 0. UD_PROVENANCE_LEDGER_ADDENDUM_SECTION_7_26_ENERGY_SOURCE_v0.1.mdUD Provenance Ledger Addendum — §7.26 Energy-Source Adjudication v0.1 Date: 2026-09-18 Physical promotion: 0 ID Object Status Claim bin ES01 external QPS calorimeter observable event heat release EMPIRICAL/SOURCE CHARACTERIZATION ES02 physical mechanism lower potential-energy valley releases ΔU\\Delta U EXTERNAL PHYSICS ES03 §7.26 physical branch ENERGY_SOURCE AUTO_LOCK SOURCE SELECTION ES04 UD scalar bridge εk=Qk/EB\\varepsilon_k=Q_k/E_B CRL-2 CANDIDATE ES05 heat variance subtraction not licensed by calorimetry source alone TYPE NO-GO ES06 dimensionless RBR_B Q1/Q0Q_1/Q_0 EXACT CONDITIONAL ES07 dimensionless D2/AD_2/A (Q2−2Q1+Q0)/Q0(Q_2-2Q_1+Q_0)/Q_0 EXACT CONDITIONAL ES08 WBX1 κ\\kappa ratio of ES07 to RB−1R_B-1 EXACT CONDITIONAL ES09 EBE_B dependence of κ\\kappa cancels AUTO_LOCK ES10 absolute εk\\varepsilon_k requires EBE_B OPEN CALIBRATION ES11 universal amplitude²→heat βobs\\beta_{\\mathrm obs} not derived / not required AUTO_LOCK NO-GO ES12 local βeff\\beta_{\\mathrm eff} state-dependent potential-curvature candidate CONDITIONAL ES13 correction #8 conditional only on future mean-amplitude branch INACTIVE FOR PHYSICAL CALORIMETRY ES14 correction #9 energy-source branch repair ERRATA LOCK UD_SECTION_7_26_BETA_CALIBRATION_AUDIT_v0.1.mdUD §7.26 Amplitude²→Energy β\\beta Calibration Audit v0.1 Date: 2026-09-18 Status: NOT REQUIRED ON SELECTED ENERGY_SOURCE LANE / UNIVERSAL BETA NO-GO Physical promotion: 0 0. Result The requested target-blind β\\beta calibration becomes unnecessary after observation-branch adjudication. The physical calorimeter measures an event energy release Q=ΔUQ=\\Delta U directly through thermometry/heat balance. It does not measure a hidden winding amplitude and then square it. Therefore a universal coefficient βobs:|w|2↦Q \\beta_{\\mathrm obs}: |w|^2\\mapsto Q is not part of the selected physical bridge. 1. Why a universal βobs\\beta_{\\mathrm obs} is not supplied by the source physics The event heat depends on the difference between device potential-energy states. In the phase-slip experiment this energy depends on quantities including: applied flux; loop inductance; critical current; phase trajectory / initial and final valleys; temperature-dependent device response. Thus the source relation is schematically Q=ΔU(ϕi,ϕf,Φx,L,Ic,T,…), Q = \\Delta U( \\phi_i,\\phi_f,\\Phi_x,L,I_c,T,\\ldots ), not Q=βobs|w|2 Q=\\beta_{\\mathrm obs}|w|^2 with a universal constant coefficient. AUTO_LOCK NO-GO UNIVERSAL_CONSTANT_AMPLITUDE_SQUARED_TO_PHASE_SLIP_HEAT_BETA_IS_NOT_DERIVED_FROM_CURRENT_CALORIMETRY_PHYSICS_v0.1 2. Local quadratic expansion does not rescue universality Around one fixed potential minimum ϕ0\\phi_0, U(ϕ0+δϕ)=U(ϕ0)+12U″(ϕ0)(δϕ)2+O(δϕ3). U(\\phi_0+\\delta\\phi) = U(\\phi_0) + \\frac12U''(\\phi_0)(\\delta\\phi)^2 + O(\\delta\\phi^3). If an independently defined winding amplitude obeyed δϕ=λw, \\delta\\phi=\\lambda w, one could define a local βeff(ϕ0)=12U″(ϕ0)λ2. \\boxed{ \\beta_{\\mathrm eff}(\\phi_0) = \\frac12U''(\\phi_0)\\lambda^2. } But this coefficient depends on the operating-point curvature U″(ϕ0)U''(\\phi_0), and therefore on the device state/parameters. It is not a universal class-independent β\\beta unless an additional theorem proves that the curvature and w→δϕw\\to\\delta\\phi map are constant over the tested classes. AUTO_LOCK LOCAL_POTENTIAL_CURVATURE_CAN_DEFINE_STATE_DEPENDENT_BETA_EFFECTIVE_BUT_NOT_UNIVERSAL_BETA_THEOREM_v0.1 3. Target-blind calibration protocol if the branch is ever reopened If a future frontier proposal insists on MEAN_AMPLITUDE_SOURCE, then before winding-response data are exposed it must independently acquire: the operational definition of ww; a calibrated map w→δϕw\\to\\delta\\phi; the device energy landscape or local curvature; temperature/flux dependence; an out-of-sample test showing one class-independent coefficient is adequate. Failure of coefficient constancy returns BETA_NOT_A_CONSTANT__USE_STATE_DEPENDENT_ENERGY_LANDSCAPE. No winding-law target may be used to choose the coefficient. 4. Notation guard The phase-slip source literature already uses βSQUID=2πLIcΦ0 \\beta_{\\mathrm SQUID} = \\frac{2\\pi LI_c}{\\Phi_0} for the magnetic screening parameter. Therefore any future amplitude²→energy bridge MUST NOT reuse the bare symbol β\\beta. Use, for example, gw2→Q g_{w^2\\to Q} or βobs \\beta_{\\mathrm obs} with explicit namespace. AUTO_LOCK NOTATION GUARD QPS_SCREENING_BETA_AND_OBSERVATION_BRIDGE_BETA_MUST_REMAIN_DISTINCT_v0.1 5. Current disposition Selected physical lane: no amplitude²→energy β\\beta required. Optional future mean-amplitude lane: source-blocked and likely state-dependent. Dimensionless κ\\kappa: obtainable from matched heat ratios/curvature without EBE_B. Absolute UD burden amplitude: still requires independent EBE_B. Physical promotion remains 0. UD_SECTION_7_26_OBSERVATION_BRANCH_ADJUDICATION_v0.1.mdUD §7.26 Observation-Branch Adjudication — Phase-Slip Calorimetry v0.1 Date: 2026-09-18 Status: ENERGY_SOURCE SELECTED FOR PHYSICAL CALORIMETRY LANE / MEAN-AMPLITUDE BRANCH INACTIVE Physical promotion: 0 0. Question The §7.26 bridge had been split into two possible observation hypotheses: ENERGY_SOURCE MEAN_AMPLITUDE_SOURCE The purpose of this audit is to determine which one is actually supported by the phase-slip calorimetry experiment used as the external physical reference. 1. External experimental object The phase-slip calorimetry experiment detects the heat released by the phase-slip event. Its physical description is an abrupt transition from a metastable/unstable phase configuration into a lower potential-energy valley. The released energy is denoted ΔU. \\Delta U. The source paper gives the phase-slip energy release in the form ΔU=Φ02πL∫Φxdϕ, \\Delta U = \\frac{\\Phi_0}{2\\pi L} \\int \\Phi_x\\,d\\phi, with a large-screening-parameter limit ΔU≈IcΦ0. \\Delta U\\approx I_c\\Phi_0. The calorimeter reconstructs the deposited heat through time-resolved electron thermometry and a thermal balance model. The measured object is therefore an energy release. No experimental relation of the form Q=βobs|w|2 Q=\\beta_{\\mathrm obs}\\,|w|^2 for a stochastic winding amplitude ww is part of the calorimetry source model. AUTO_LOCK SOURCE CHARACTERIZATION PHASE_SLIP_NANOCALORIMETER_NATIVE_OBSERVABLE_IS_EVENT_HEAT_RELEASE_NOT_MEAN_WINDING_AMPLITUDE_SQUARED_v0.1 2. §7.26 branch ruling For the physical calorimetry lane, select 𝙴𝙽𝙴𝚁𝙶𝚈_𝚂𝙾𝚄𝚁𝙲𝙴. \\boxed{\\texttt{ENERGY_SOURCE}}. The UD bridge candidate is therefore εk=QkEB, \\boxed{ \\varepsilon_k = \\frac{Q_k}{E_B}, } where QkQ_k is the source-isolated class heat and EBE_B is a common energy-to-native-burden normalization if absolute burden units are required. This remains a UD bridge hypothesis; the external experiment establishes QkQ_k as heat, not the identity of heat with UD burden. AUTO_FREEZE AS DEFAULT PHYSICAL-CALORIMETRY INTERPRETATION MEAN_AMPLITUDE_SOURCE_USED_AS_DEFAULT_INTERPRETATION_OF_PHASE_SLIP_CALORIMETRY_v0.1 The mean-amplitude branch may be studied separately only after an independent theorem maps a declared winding amplitude to physical dissipated heat. 3. Consequence for variance Under ENERGY_SOURCE, run-to-run variation of measured heat is part of the empirical distribution of the energy observable unless a separately validated measurement/noise model decomposes it into nuisance and physical components. Therefore Var(Qk) \\operatorname{Var}(Q_k) must be retained for: uncertainty of the class mean; covariance propagation; heteroscedasticity diagnostics; leakage/confounding analysis. But it must not be subtracted deterministically from the class mean merely because the calorimeter is ultimately an energy detector. In particular, the identity 𝔼[w2]=|𝔼w|2+Var(w) \\mathbb E[w^2] = |\\mathbb Ew|^2+\\operatorname{Var}(w) does not authorize Qk↦Qk−βVar(wk) Q_k\\mapsto Q_k-\\beta\\operatorname{Var}(w_k) unless the missing physical bridge Q=β|w|2 Q=\\beta|w|^2 has first been established. AUTO_LOCK TYPE GUARD AMPLITUDE_VARIANCE_SUBTRACTION_IS_NOT_LICENSED_ON_ENERGY_SOURCE_CALORIMETRY_BRANCH_WITHOUT_AMPLITUDE_TO_HEAT_THEOREM_v0.1 4. Winding discriminator on the energy branch For a common class-independent energy scale, εk=Qk/EB. \\varepsilon_k=Q_k/E_B. Then RB=ε1ε0=Q1Q0. \\boxed