k=bk−ak, I_k=[a_k,b_k], \\qquad \\ell_k=b_k-a_k, define xk=12π∫Ikqdx. x_k = \\frac1{2\\pi}\\int_{I_k}q\\,dx. Define the arc-mean phase gradient q‾k=1ℓk∫Ikqdx=2πxkℓk. \\bar q_k = \\frac1{\\ell_k} \\int_{I_k}q\\,dx = \\frac{2\\pi x_k}{\\ell_k}. Write q=q‾k+δqk, q = \\bar q_k+\\delta q_k, with ∫Ikδqkdx=0. \\int_{I_k}\\delta q_k\\,dx=0. Also define W:=F2, W:=F^2, Q0k:=∫IkWdx, Q_{0k} := \\int_{I_k}W\\,dx, Q1k:=∫IkWδqkdx, Q_{1k} := \\int_{I_k}W\\,\\delta q_k\\,dx, Q2k:=∫IkW(δqk)2dx, Q_{2k} := \\int_{I_k}W\\,(\\delta q_k)^2dx, and Pk:=∫Ik[Fx2−νF2+12F4]dx. P_k := \\int_{I_k} \\left[ F_x^2 -\\nu F^2 +\\frac12F^4 \\right]dx. Then exactly, ∫IkF2q2dx=q‾k2Q0k+2q‾kQ1k+Q2k. \\int_{I_k}F^2q^2dx = \\bar q_k^2Q_{0k} + 2\\bar q_kQ_{1k} + Q_{2k}. Therefore ℱk=4π2Q0kℓk2xk2+4πQ1kℓkxk+Q2k+Pk. \\boxed{ \\mathcal F_k = \\frac{4\\pi^2Q_{0k}}{\\ell_k^2}x_k^2 + \\frac{4\\pi Q_{1k}}{\\ell_k}x_k + Q_{2k} + P_k. } This is the exact coarse/kernel decomposition. 4. Generic factorization obstruction A strict additive factorization ℱ=ℱC4(x)+ℱker(z) \\mathcal F = \\mathcal F_{C_4}(x) + \\mathcal F_{\\ker}(z) requires that hidden coordinates zz not alter the xx-dependent terms. But generically: Q0k=Q0k[F] Q_{0k}=Q_{0k}[F] depends on the unresolved amplitude profile, and Q1k=∫F2δqkdx Q_{1k} = \\int F^2\\delta q_k\\,dx is nonzero whenever amplitude and sub-arc phase-gradient fluctuations are correlated. Thus the hidden sector changes the quadratic coarse coefficient 4π2Q0kℓk2 \\frac{4\\pi^2Q_{0k}}{\\ell_k^2} and generates the explicit coarse/kernel cross term 4πQ1kℓkxk. \\frac{4\\pi Q_{1k}}{\\ell_k}x_k. Hence ℱphys≠κAℱC4(x)+ℱker(z) \\boxed{ \\mathcal F_{\\mathrm phys} \\neq \\kappa_A\\mathcal F_{C_4}(x) + \\mathcal F_{\\ker}(z) } with fixed κA\\kappa_A on the generic TDGL state space. This is stronger than the prior C4-PROJ failure: hidden amplitude structure not only changes the coarse velocity; it enters the coarse energy coefficient itself. 5. Explicit same-xx, different-energy witness Take one arc of