    "content": "Locks a common branch-contrast reporting language for Córdoba and Lehigh while keeping carriers, calibrations, instruments, uncertainty, and verdicts platform-specific. JOP v2.40 Addendum — Cross-Platform QTP Branch-Contrast Replication Grammar v0.1 A common reporting grammar is frozen for the independent University of Córdoba and Lehigh/Bitlismen quadruple-tank platforms. For each typed platform pp, Cbr(p)=Δq1(p)−Δq2(p), C_{\\mathrm br}^{(p)}=\\Delta q_1^{(p)}-\\Delta q_2^{(p)}, G14(p)=14Cbr(p),G23(p)=−G14(p). G_{14}^{(p)}=\\frac14C_{\\mathrm br}^{(p)}, \\qquad G_{23}^{(p)}=-G_{14}^{(p)}. The common relation does not identify the two experimental carriers. Instrumentation, calibration, excitation, sampling, and uncertainty remain independently sourced. The reporting ladder distinguishes: DUAL_SOURCE_LAW_REPLAY_PASS: both physical QTPs instantiate the exact source law; ONE_SITE_PHYSICAL_COMPARATOR_PASS: Córdoba passes its independently frozen flowmeter-versus-level comparator while Lehigh only instantiates the source law; DUAL_PHYSICAL_COMPARATOR_REPLICATION_PASS: both platforms pass independently preregistered physical comparators under their own pretarget uncertainty gates. No cross-platform amplitude equality, pooled statistic, fitted normalization, or one-site calibration transfer is permitted. Equal formulas do not imply equal experimental objects. At the current freeze, Córdoba’s fresh raw data and metrology receipts remain pending, while Lehigh’s delivered-flow provenance remains pending and its independent physical comparator is open. Physical promotion remains zero."
