    "content": "Defines the source-replay, one-site comparator, and dual-comparator reporting ladder without pooling statistics or transferring calibration between platforms. UD QTP Cross-Platform Branch-Contrast Replication Preregistration v0.1 Generated: 2026-09-09T02:14:28.325392+00:00 Status: PRETARGET_FROZEN / TWO-PLATFORM REPORTING GRAMMAR LOCKED Claim class: CROSS_PLATFORM_REPLICATION_PROTOCOL Physical promotion: 0 0. Purpose Unify the Córdoba and Lehigh quadruple-tank lanes under one reporting grammar without merging their carriers, calibrations, instruments, timing rules, or uncertainty models. The common source object is the typed delivered-flow branch contrast. For each platform pp, Cbr(p):=Δq1(p)−Δq2(p) \\boxed{ C_{\\mathrm br}^{(p)} := \\Delta q_1^{(p)}-\\Delta q_2^{(p)} } and G14(p)=Cbr(p)4,G23(p)=−Cbr(p)4. \\boxed{ G_{14}^{(p)} = \\frac{C_{\\mathrm br}^{(p)}}4, \\qquad G_{23}^{(p)} = -\\frac{C_{\\mathrm br}^{(p)}}4. } Typed provenance is mandatory: Cbr(CORDOBA)≠Cbr(LEHIGH) C_{\\mathrm br}^{(\\mathrm{CORDOBA})} \\neq C_{\\mathrm br}^{(\\mathrm{LEHIGH})} as experimental objects even when numerical values happen to agree. The factor 1/41/4 is the common frozen source law. Instrument scale, run amplitude, sampling cadence, calibration, uncertainty, and physical target remain platform-specific. 1. Platform A — Córdoba Source observable Direct electromagnetic-flowmeter channels: fLmeter,fRmeter. f_L^{\\mathrm meter},\\qquad f_R^{\\mathrm meter}. The frozen two-state source contrast is Cbr(CORDOBA)=ΔfLmeter−ΔfRmeter. C_{\\mathrm br}^{(\\mathrm{CORDOBA})} = \\Delta f_L^{\\mathrm meter} - \\Delta f_R^{\\mathrm meter}. The source edge component is G14,src(CORDOBA)=Cbr(CORDOBA)4. G_{14,\\mathrm src}^{(\\mathrm{CORDOBA})} = \\frac{C_{\\mathrm br}^{(\\mathrm{CORDOBA})}}4. Independent same-apparatus comparator The already-frozen level-slope lane supplies G14,level(CORDOBA) G_{14,\\mathrm level}^{(\\mathrm{CORDOBA})} and R14(CORDOBA)=G14,level(CORDOBA)−G14,src(CORDOBA). R_{14}^{(\\mathrm{CORDOBA})} = G_{14,\\mathrm level}^{(\\mathrm{CORDOBA})} - G_{14,\\mathrm src}^{(\\mathrm{CORDOBA})}. The numerical PASS/FAIL gate remains source-blocked until authenticated installed-instrument metrology closes. No change to the Córdoba scorer or its uncertainty rules is made by this cross-platform protocol. 2. Platform B — Lehigh / InTaSet Source observable The source scorer uses either: direct authenticated delivered-flow channels; or an authenticated physical command-to-delivered-flow calibration. For adjacent source rows n−1,nn-1,n, Cbr(LEHIGH)[n]=Δq1[n]−Δq2[n]. C_{\\mathrm br}^{(\\mathrm{LEHIGH})}[n] = \\Delta q_1[n]-\\Delta q_2[n]. Then G14,src(LEHIGH)[n]=Cbr(LEHIGH)[n]4, G_{14,\\mathrm src}^{(\\mathrm{LEHIGH})}[n] = \\frac{C_{\\mathrm br}^{(\\mathrm{LEHIGH})}[n]}4, G23,src(LEHIGH)[n]=−G14,src(LEHIGH)[n]. G_{23,\\mathrm src}^{(\\mathrm{LEHIGH})}[n] = -G_{14,\\mathrm src}^{(\\mathrm{LEHIGH})}[n]. Tank 1–4 outcomes are not read by the frozen Lehigh source scorer. Independent comparator No Lehigh physical comparator is introduced here. Current status: LEHIGH_INDEPENDENT_COMPARATOR := OPEN A future Lehigh comparator must be: independently sourced; separately preregistered before outcome scoring; barred from fitting the Pump command→flow calibration; given its own pretarget uncertainty gate. Until that occurs, a Lehigh source-stream execution is not promoted to physical validation. 3. Common reporting object For every platform, report the following typed fields. A. Provenance platform_id apparatus_source source_protocol_sha256 raw_source_sha256 configuration_id flow_source_mode flow_units source_receipt_status B. Source-law realization contrast_definition transition_definition N_source_contrasts C_branch records or frozen two-state value G14_source G23_source max_abs_identity_residual = max |G14_source + G23_source| The identity residual is an implementation check only. C. Independent physical comparator comparator_status comparator_definition R14 uncertainty_mode threshold platform_verdict If no independent comparator exists: comparator_status := OPEN R14 := null threshold := null platform_verdict := NO_PHYSICAL_COMPARATOR_VERDICT D. Claim boundary physical_promotion := 0 4. Frozen cross-platform status ladder Status S1 — DUAL_SOURCE_LAW_REPLAY_PASS Allowed iff: Córdoba source stream/result is source-authenticated; Lehigh source stream is source-authenticated; both independently reproduce G14+G23=0 G_{14}+G_{23}=0 exactly or to the frozen implementation precision; neither uses outcome-fitted calibration. Meaning: the same exact branch-contrast source law has been instantiated on two independent physical QTP platforms. Not allowed meaning: the law has been independently physically validated. This status is still an exact-source realization because the G14/G23G_{14}/G_{23} antisymmetry is algebraically generated from the source contrast. Status S2 — ONE_SITE_PHYSICAL_COMPARATOR_PASS Allowed iff: S1 holds, and Córdoba passes its frozen independent flowmeter-versus-level comparator, while Lehigh’s independent comparator remains OPEN. Meaning: one independent QTP platform has passed a same-apparatus physical comparator and the second platform has independently instantiated the source law. This is not called independent physical replication. Status S3 — DUAL_PHYSICAL_COMPARATOR_REPLICATION_PASS Allowed iff: S1 holds; Córdoba passes its separately frozen independent comparator; Lehigh has a separately preregistered independent comparator; Lehigh passes its own platform-specific pretarget uncertainty gate; neither platform’s threshold, calibration, window, or comparator was altered after outcome exposure. Only S3 licenses the phrase: independent cross-platform physical comparator replication within the tested QTP scope. 5. Cross-platform quantities that are NOT compared The following are explicitly not replication targets: Cbr(CORDOBA)=Cbr(LEHIGH), C_{\\mathrm br}^{(\\mathrm{CORDOBA})} = C_{\\mathrm br}^{(\\mathrm{LEHIGH})}, G14(CORDOBA)=G14(LEHIGH), G_{14}^{(\\mathrm{CORDOBA})} = G_{14}^{(\\mathrm{LEHIGH})}, mean amplitudes, RMS amplitudes, zero-event rates, command magnitudes, sampling rates, or tank trajectories. Why: experiments may use different excitation schedules; sampling intervals differ; actuator calibrations differ; physical plant geometry and hydraulic parameters differ; one site measures flow directly while the other may require a calibration receipt. No amplitude pooling is permitted without a separately derived cross-platform normalization. 6. No pooled statistic No meta-analytic, averaged, weighted, standardized, z-scored, normalized, or concatenated cross-platform scalar is defined in v0.1. Specifically barred: POOLED_G14 := PROHIBITED POOLED_R14 := PROHIBITED CROSS_PLATFORM_Z_SCORE := PROHIBITED TARGET_SELECTED_NORMALIZATION := PROHIBITED ONE_PLATFORM_USED_TO_CALIBRATE_THE_OTHER := PROHIBITED The two platform reports are presented side by side. 7. Missing-platform rule If one platform remains source-blocked, the report must retain the blocked result. Examples: CORDOBA := DATA_BLOCKED LEHIGH := SOURCE_BLOCKED CROSS_PLATFORM_STATUS := INCOMPLETE A passing site cannot rescue a blocked or failed site. 8. Failure rule If a platform fails its own frozen independent comparator, preserve that result. No cross-platform aggregate may override it. Examples: CORDOBA := EXECUTION_FAIL LEHIGH := SOURCE_STREAM_GENERATED CROSS_PLATFORM_STATUS := PHYSICAL_COMPARATOR_FAIL or, once both comparators exist, CORDOBA := EXECUTION_PASS LEHIGH := EXECUTION_FAIL CROSS_PLATFORM_STATUS := DUAL_PHYSICAL_REPLICATION_FAIL 9. Independent implementation requirement Each platform keeps its own dual-scorer or independent replay requirement. The cross-platform reporter does not recompute source physics. It reads frozen site result artifacts and checks only: schema; provenance hashes; typed status; common source-law identity field; cross-platform status-ladder logic. 10. Current pretarget disposition At freeze time: CORDOBA: source apparatus := QUALIFIED fresh raw data := PENDING installed accuracy receipts := PENDING independent comparator := FROZEN / NOT EXECUTED LEHIGH: source workbook := AUTHENTICATED physical delivered-flow calibration/direct telemetry := PENDING source scorer := FROZEN / NOT PHYSICALLY EXECUTED independent comparator := OPEN CROSS_PLATFORM_STATUS := INCOMPLETE PHYSICAL_PROMOTION := 0 No fresh physical outcome from either pending lane is included in this preregistration."
