law Vi=Vi(hi) V_i=V_i(h_i) on the experimental level domain. Define the differential storage capacity Ki(hi):=dVidhi. \\boxed{ K_i(h_i):=\\frac{dV_i}{dh_i}. } Then the level-derived storage-rate channel is V̇i=Ki(hi)ḣi. \\boxed{ \\dot V_i = K_i(h_i)\\dot h_i. } This formulation does not assume that the tanks are cylindrical or share equal cross-sectional areas. Constant-area specialization Only if a source geometry receipt states that the relevant tank region has constant area AiA_i, Vi(hi)=Aihi+Vi,0, V_i(h_i)=A_i h_i+V_{i,0}, then Ki(hi)=Ai \\boxed{ K_i(h_i)=A_i } and V̇i=Aiḣi. \\dot V_i=A_i\\dot h_i. No Córdoba tank areas, Johansson parameters, numerical-QTP areas, photograph scaling, or generic Bitlismen dimensions may populate this source slot. 3. Frozen hydraulic isolation configuration A scored run must use a source-declared configuration in which all non-pump tank flows entering the storage balance are either: A. physically closed / isolated, or B. independently measured and included as predeclared correction channels. The preferred v0.1 comparator is Mode A: physical isolation. Mode A — fill isolation Before target acquisition, the source/operator receipt must identify the physical valve state showing that, during each scored fill window: pump inlet path is enabled as declared; tank outlet-to-reservoir paths are closed; upper-to-lower/intertank gravity-transfer paths are closed; alternate/bypass outlet paths are closed; no unmeasured drain, overflow, or recirculation path is active. Under this declared configuration: q1,rtank=V̇1,r+V̇4,r, \\boxed{ q_{1,r}^{\\mathrm tank} = \\dot V_{1,r}+\\dot V_{4,r}, } q2,rtank=V̇2,r+V̇3,r. \\boxed{ q_{2,r}^{\\mathrm tank} = \\dot V_{2,r}+\\dot V_{3,r}. } The pump split fractions inside each branch are irrelevant because the two tank storage rates are summed. Mode B — corrected mass balance Mode B is not executable in v0.1. If the physical rig cannot isolate the non-pump flows, every remaining inflow/outflow term must be independently measured or source-modeled in a separately versioned protocol before scoring. No generic Torricelli coefficient, outlet-orifice area, discharge coefficient, or numerical-model parameter may be inserted into v0.1. 4. Two-state fresh experiment Use two source-declared, non-overlapping fill windows: r∈{0,1}. r\\in\\{0,1\\}. The pump source channel provides independently authenticated delivered-flow states q1,0flow,q1,1flow, q_{1,0}^{\\mathrm flow},\\quad q_{1,1}^{\\mathrm flow}, q2,0flow,q2,1flow. q_{2,0}^{\\mathrm flow},\\quad q_{2,1}^{\\mathrm flow}. The tank-side channel is derived independently from level and geometry. For general geometry, define the window-average tank storage rate V̇‾i,r=1|Wr|∑n∈WrKi(hi,n)ḣi,n, \\bar{\\dot V}_{i,r} = \\frac1{|W_r|} \\sum_{n\\in W_r} K_i(h_{i,n})\\dot h_{i,n}, using the frozen level-derivative estimator and source geometry law. Then q1,rtank=V̇‾1,r+V̇‾4,r, q_{1,r}^{\\mathrm tank} = \\bar{\\dot V}_{1,r} + \\bar{\\dot V}_{4,r}, q2,rtank=V̇‾2,r+V̇‾3,r. q_{2,r}^{\\mathrm tank} = \\bar{\\dot V}_{2,r} + \\bar{\\dot V}_{3,r}. Constant-area linear-fill specialization If geometry is constant-area and each source-declared fill window is admitted as linear, mi,r=dhidt|Wr, m_{i,r} = \\frac{d h_i}{dt}\\Big|_{W_r}, then q1,rtank=A1m1,r+A4m4,r, \\boxed{ q_{1,r}^{\\mathrm tank} = A_1m_{1,r}+A_4m_{4,r}, } q2,rtank=A2m2,r+A3m3,r. \\boxed{ q_{2,r}^{\\mathrm tank} = A_2m_{2,r}+A_3m_{3,r}. } This specialization is closest to the already frozen Córdoba comparator but remains a distinct Lehigh experimental object with independently sourced geometry and uncertainty. 5. Independent Lehigh target Define Δq1tank=q1,1tank−q1,0tank, \\Delta q_1^{\\mathrm tank} = q_{1,1}^{\\mathrm tank}-q_{1,0}^{\\mathrm tank}, Δq2tank=q2,1tank−q2,0tank. \\Delta q_2^{\\mathrm tank} = q_{2,1}^{\\mathrm tank}-q_{2,0}^{\\mathrm tank}. The tank-side target is G14,tank(LEHIGH)=Δq1tank−Δq2tank4. \\boxed{ G_{14,\\mathrm tank}^{(\\mathrm{LEHIGH})} = \\frac{ \\Delta q_1^{\\mathrm tank} - \\Delta q_2^{\\mathrm tank} }{4}. } The independently sourced pump-flow prediction is G14,flow(LEHIGH)=Δq1flow−Δq2flow4. \\boxed{ G_{14,\\mathrm flow}^{(\\mathrm{LEHIGH})} = \\frac{ \\Delta q_1^{\\mathrm flow} - \\Delta q_2^{\\mathrm flow} }{4}. } Primary physical residual: R14(LEHIGH)=G14,tank(LEHIGH)−G14,flow(LEHIGH). \\boxed{ R_{14}^{(\\mathrm{LEHIGH})} = G_{14,\\mathrm tank}^{(\\mathrm{LEHIGH})} - G_{14,\\mathrm flow}^{(\\mathrm{LEHIGH})}. } This is not the identity G14=−G23G_{14}=-G_{23} computed twice from the same flow source. It compares pump-side delivered-flow provenance with an independent tank storage-rate measurement path. 6. Exact branch-closure decomposition At state rr, define typed branch closure receipts B1,r=q1,rtank−q1,rflow, B_{1,r} = q_{1,r}^{\\mathrm tank} - q_{1,r}^{\\mathrm flow}, B2,r=q2,rtank−q2,rflow. B_{2,r} = q_{2,r}^{\\mathrm tank} - q_{2,r}^{\\mathrm flow}. Then exactly R14(LEHIGH)=(B1,1−B1,0)−(B2,1−B2,0)4. \\boxed{ R_{14}^{(\\mathrm{LEHIGH})} = \\frac{ (B_{1,1}-B_{1,0}) - (B_{2,1}-B_{2,0}) }{4}. } This decomposition is independent of the internal pump split parameters. 7. Pretarget window rule Before opening the fresh target channel, freeze: run ID; configuration ID; source geometry receipt; valve/isolation state; pump-flow calibration/direct-flow receipt; pump state 0 and state 1; transient exclusion interval; level-fit duration; derivative/slope estimator; uncertainty model and PASS band. No window may move after inspecting R14R_{14}. 8. Isolation qualification gate The operator/source must provide an explicit pretarget isolation receipt. Required fields: pump1_to_tanks_1_4 := confirmed pump2_to_tanks_2_3 := confirmed tank_outlet_to_reservoir_paths := CLOSED intertank_gravity_transfer_paths := CLOSED alternate_upper_outlet_paths := CLOSED unmeasured_bypass_paths := NONE / CLOSED overflow_possible_in_fit_windows := FALSE If a physical path cannot be classified from the source/operator configuration: SOURCE_BLOCKED