    "size_bytes": 0,
    "content": "Ranks and types an alternate time-resolved source path, including its temporal-seat construction, nulls, data-volume feasibility, and representation limitation. Open-Raw Alternate Physical Source to ST3S — TTRTS v0.1 Date: 2026-09-10 Result: CANDIDATE SELECTED / OPEN RAW SOURCE EXISTS / BYTES NOT MATERIALIZED IN THIS RUNTIME Candidate: Temporal-Triplet Random Telegraph Source (TTRTS) Primary corpus: University of Southampton D1488 Physical promotion: 0 1. Selection result The brightest independent physical-source alternative found with an already open raw event corpus is TTRTS-D1488 \\boxed{ \\text{TTRTS-D1488} } built from the open Southampton dataset accompanying: Ibukuro et al., Silicon single-electron random number generator based on random telegraph signals at room temperature, AIP Advances 10, 115101 (2020). The paper reports nine time-domain RTS measurements acquired at one fixed bias condition. Each run contains 100001 \\boxed{100001} samples at native sampling interval tint=24ms, \\boxed{t_{\\mathrm int}=24~{\\mathrm ms}}, for total duration 100001×24ms=2400.024s 100001\\times24~{\\mathrm ms} = 2400.024~{\\mathrm s} per run. The article reports approximately 2400 s and uses a 20 s hold between measurements, longer than the typical RTS lifetime, to suppress inter-run autocorrelation. Seven runs are used for classifier/training extraction and two are reserved as test runs in the published analysis. The supporting D1488 data are stated by the authors to be openly available in the University of Southampton repository. 2. Physical source The measured RTS is not a software-loaded bit pattern. The device is a silicon single-electron-pump / quantum-dot structure in which discrete current states arise from stochastic trapping and detrapping of an electron. The publication explicitly describes RTS as an unpredictable/stochastic physical process and observes average state lifetimes of order one second. For the RNG experiment, the high-current state is mapped to digital 1 and the lower current state(s) to digital 0 using a classifier derived from separate training measurements. Thus D1488 has a stronger natural-source provenance than pulse-programmed qubit datasets. 3. Temporal-seat construction TTRTS does not pretend that one physical trap contains three simultaneous spatial coordinates. Instead, after calibration-only digitization and resampling, let br,k∈{0,1} b_{r,k}\\in\\{0,1\\} be the physical RTS bit at resampled index kk in held-out run rr. Form non-overlapping three-seat physical state records Br,n=(br,3n,br,3n+1,br,3n+2). \\boxed{ B_{r,n} = (b_{r,3n},b_{r,3n+1},b_{r,3n+2}). } Define the transition receipt Ar,n=Br,n−1⊕Br,n,n≥1. \\boxed{ A_{r,n} = B_{r,n-1}\\oplus B_{r,n}, \\qquad n\\ge1. } Therefore each scored event produces exactly the same typed data format needed by the source correspondence lane: BB: three-bit state; AA: three-bit transition receipt. The physical coordinates are typed as: temporal seats (0,1,2), \\boxed{ \\text{temporal seats }(0,1,2), } not spatial dots, not tetrahedral matching classes, and not independently existing particles. 4. Calibration-only digitization Use only the seven preregistered calibration runs: D1,…,D7. D1,\\dots,D7. Freeze from those runs: current-state classifier / threshold; accepted current range; typical high/low state lifetimes; resampling stride qq; temporal guard for the later correspondence null. The published procedure defines a typical RTS lifetime τ=max(τHigh,τLow) \\tau=\\max(\\tau_{\\mathrm High},\\tau_{\\mathrm Low}) and a resampling time T=2τ T=2\\tau to reduce autocorrelation. The candidate adapter mirrors this source-side rule. With native 24 ms sampling, freeze q=max(1,⌊T/tint⌋) \\boxed{ q=\\max\\left(1,\\left\\lfloor T/t_{\\mathrm int}\\right\\rfloor\\right) } from calibration only. Use one fixed sampling phase: k0=0. \\boxed{k_0=0.} The paper explored multiple possible initial resampling offsets for RNG analysis; TTRTS deliberately does not search over offsets because selecting the best phase after comparison would be a hidden fit. 5. Held-out corpus Freeze: D1–D7: calibration only; D8–D9: held-out physical source only. The numerical labels are the partition rule. No trace is selected because of its agreement with UD. For each held-out run: apply the frozen classifier; resample at stride qq from phase zero; form non-overlapping triplets BB; form transition receipts AA; retain the native run boundary. No event is moved across D8/D9. 6. Data-volume feasibility The paper reports that the training-derived resampling ratio was approximately T/tint∼55. T/t_{\\mathrm int}\\sim55. If the frozen calibration returns q=55q=55, one 100001-point run gives ⌊10000055⌋+1=1819 \\left\\lfloor\\frac{100000}{55}\\right\\rfloor+1 = 1819 resampled physical bits. This yields ⌊18193⌋=606 \\left\\lfloor\\frac{1819}{3}\\right\\rfloor = 606 three-seat state records and therefore 605 \\boxed{605} state/transition events per held-out run. Two held-out runs would then provide 1210 \\boxed{1210} physical TTRTS events before any additional quality exclusions. This calculation is a corpus-feasibility estimate based on the reported approximate resampling ratio. The actual qq must be recalculated from the raw calibration files and frozen before held-out scoring. 7. Block-preserving temporal null Because D8 and D9 are separate physical acquisitions with a 20 s hold between them, the candidate correspondence test must preserve run boundaries. For held-out blocks r∈{8,9}r\\in\\{8,9\\}, let allowed circular shifts be 𝒟r={d:1≤d<Nr,min(d,Nr−d)>Gr}, \\mathcal D_r = \\{d:1\\le d<N_r,\\ \\min(d,N_r-d)>G_r\\}, with GrG_r frozen from calibration. For each pair (d8,d9)∈𝒟8×𝒟9, (d_8,d_9)\\in\\mathcal D_8\\times\\mathcal D_9, shift each physical block only inside itself, sum the two block statistics, and compare with the unshifted two-block score. This gives an exact product-shift temporal null while preserving: each run’s physical sequence; each run’s UD sequence; within-run temporal structure; the acquisition boundary. No circular shift is allowed across D8/D9. 8. Address-level null The existing shell-conditioned address null remains mandatory. Within each held-out run and each physical shell pair (wH(A),wH(B)), (w_H(A),w_H(B)), randomize complete physical six-bit records only among events in the same shell-pair stratum. Thus Hamming-level agreement cannot masquerade as coordinate-address correspondence. 9. Critical representation limitation TTRTS is a weaker physical ontology than ST3S. ST3S has three simultaneous spatial sites and admits a natural candidate for physical coordinate permutation. TTRTS has three time seats produced by one stochastic physical source. Therefore: TTRTS temporal-seat permutation≠physical S3 spatial symmetry. \\boxed{ \\text{TTRTS temporal-seat permutation} \\neq \\text{physical }S_3\\text{ spatial symmetry}. } At most, stationarity and successful randomness/decorrelation tests can support an empirical seat exchangeability approximation. They cannot establish an exact physical identity with the three UD matching coordinates. This limitation is not repaired by a statistically significant correspondence score. 10. Candidate hierarchy Rank 1 — D1488 TTRTS-SEP Strengths - open data; - nine long raw time-domain measurements; - known native sample interval and run length; - natural stochastic single-electron physics; - calibration/test structure already documented; - enough apparent data volume for a frozen held-out source test. Weakness - three coordinates are temporal seats rather than spatial source sites. Disposition BRIGHTEST OPEN-RAW ALTERNATE / CANDIDATE-B SOURCE ONTOLOGY. Rank 2 — D1193 single-dopant RTS Open 21 MB dataset from a low-temperature MOSFET where RTS is attributed to trapping/detrapping at a solitary donor. This has even cleaner single-defect source semantics, but the public search result does not expose enough file-level temporal structure to certify the v0.1 data-volume/adapter contract without opening the archive. Disposition SOURCE-PURITY LEADER / FILE-SEMANTICS INSPECTION REQUIRED. Rank 3 — D1378 thesis archive Open thesis-support archive containing published and unpublished RTS data. This may contain additional useful natural event streams but requires archive inspection before a specific replay lane can be frozen. Disposition OPEN ARCHIVE RESERVE. 11. Runtime source status The Southampton repository records are openly licensed and downloadable, but the repository page returned HTTP 403 to this runtime when opened directly. Therefore: PUBLIC SOURCE CONFIRMED \\boxed{ \\text{PUBLIC SOURCE CONFIRMED} } but RAW BYTES NOT MATERIALIZED / NOT SCORED. \\boxed{ \\text{RAW BYTES NOT MATERIALIZED / NOT SCORED}. } No empirical TTRTS/UD correspondence result is claimed in this release. 12. Scientific disposition EXACT - temporal-triplet state/transition transform; - event-count arithmetic conditional on qq; - block-preserving null construction. EMPIRICAL - D1488 contains long natural RTS time-domain measurements and is publicly deposited; - D1193 is an open single-dopant RTS dataset. CANDIDATE - TTRTS temporal-seat physical source representation. NO-GO - temporal seats retyped as exact spatial S3S_3 coordinates; - resampling phase optimized after UD comparison; - author RNG output substituted for source-side raw calibration without provenance audit. SOURCE-BLOCKED IN CURRENT RUNTIME - raw D1488/D1193 bytes not materialized. PHYSICAL PROMOTION := 0."
