en the first-order delta-method map is D=diag(1/Je), D=\\operatorname{diag}(1/J_e), because ze=ln(|Je|/2). z_e=\\ln(|J_e|/2). Hence ΣT≈DΣJD𝖳. \\boxed{\\Sigma_T\\approx D\\Sigma_JD^\\mathsf T}. This lane is DERIVED_FIRST_ORDER unless the lab explicitly certifies it. Direct covariance of transformed log-current replicates is preferred. Root/reference covariance For held-out magnitudes, the root parity gauge cancels exactly because H=CSH=CS. Root-probe covariance is therefore not part of ΣH=CΣTC𝖳\\Sigma_H=C\\Sigma_TC^\\mathsf T. Root-probe uncertainty remains load-bearing for unique individual support coordinates and signed-amplitude reconstruction. QuiX source status The current runtime contains an intentionally incomplete QuiX calibration template: detector uncertainty, session identity, certificates, and hashes are not yet populated. No signed/session-specific 14-by-14 QuiX current covariance is present. Accordingly: 𝚀𝚄𝙸𝚇_𝙽𝚄𝙼𝙴𝚁𝙸𝙲𝙰𝙻_𝙿𝚁𝙴𝙳𝙸𝙲𝚃𝙸𝙾𝙽_𝙸𝙽𝚃𝙴𝚁𝚅𝙰𝙻𝚂=𝚂𝙾𝚄𝚁𝙲𝙴_𝙸𝙽𝙲𝙾𝙼𝙿𝙻𝙴𝚃𝙴. \\boxed{\\texttt{QUIX\\_NUMERICAL\\_PREDICTION\\_INTERVALS=SOURCE\\_INCOMPLETE}}. The propagation law and admission schema are frozen before device data exposure. PHYSICAL PROMOTION=0. \\boxed{\\text{PHYSICAL PROMOTION}=0}."
