    "content": "Formalizes the one-parameter through-origin fits, absolute adequacy gate, strong-selection gate, and non-promotion boundary. UD Empirical Joint Source-Event Scorer v0.2 — Frozen Theorem and Decision Rule Status: FROZEN PRE-HARDWARE-UNBLIND / NO HARDWARE ENDPOINTS SCORED Primary dataset: six balanced blocks, exactly 12 valid E0E_0 and 12 valid E1E_1 events Models: PLB1 vs HCB1 Physical promotion: 0 1. Inputs For each valid unblinded run ii, the scorer consumes independently returned: εi,uε,i,Λi,uΛ,i,cov(εi,Λi), \\varepsilon_i,\\quad u_{\\varepsilon,i},\\quad \\Lambda_i,\\quad u_{\\Lambda,i},\\quad \\operatorname{cov}(\\varepsilon_i,\\Lambda_i), plus event label E0E_0 or E1E_1, block index, custody/calibration/source-purity gates and units. No empirical tolerance is chosen after outcome exposure. 2. Frozen sample gate The primary score requires exactly N0=N1=12 \\boxed{N_0=N_1=12} valid events arranged as six blocks with exactly two valid E0E_0 and two valid E1E_1 events per block. Preregistered invalid hardware/receipt runs are retained in the archive and replaced append-only until the primary balanced set is complete. 3. PLB1 empirical model εi=κPΛi. \\boxed{\\varepsilon_i=\\kappa_P\\Lambda_i.} For a proposed κP\\kappa_P, the propagated residual variance is vP,i(κP)=uε,i2+κP2uΛ,i2−2κPcov(εi,Λi). \\boxed{ v_{P,i}(\\kappa_P)= u_{\\varepsilon,i}^2+ \\kappa_P^2u_{\\Lambda,i}^2- 2\\kappa_P\\operatorname{cov}(\\varepsilon_i,\\Lambda_i). } The channel covariance must be supplied explicitly. Interface-level independence normally implies zero covariance, but the scorer never silently inserts zero. The fitted κ̂P\\hat\\kappa_P minimizes the Gaussian negative log-likelihood ℒP(κP)=12∑i[log(2πvP,i)+(εi−κPΛi)2vP,i]. \\mathcal L_P(\\kappa_P)= \\frac12\\sum_i\\left[ \\log(2\\pi v_{P,i})+ \\frac{(\\varepsilon_i-\\kappa_P\\Lambda_i)^2}{v_{P,i}} \\right]. No intercept and no extra between-run noise parameter are fitted. 4. HCB1 empirical model Define the exact structural predictor di={1/4,E0,3/4,E1. d_i=\\begin{cases} 1/4,&E_0,\\\\ 3/4,&E_1. \\end{cases} HCB1 is εi=κHdi. \\boxed{\\varepsilon_i=\\kappa_H d_i.} with vH,i=uε,i2. v_{H,i}=u_{\\varepsilon,i}^2. The through-origin weighted estimate is κ̂H=∑idiεi/uε,i2∑idi2/uε,i2. \\boxed{ \\hat\\kappa_H= \\frac{\\sum_i d_i\\varepsilon_i/u_{\\varepsilon,i}^2} {\\sum_i d_i^2/u_{\\varepsilon,i}^2}. } No intercept or extra noise term is allowed. 5. Absolute goodness-of-fit gate For either model MM, define χM2=∑irM,i2vM,i. \\chi_M^2=\\sum_i\\frac{r_{M,i}^2}{v_{M,i}}. Each model has one fitted parameter, so ν=24−1=23. \\nu=24-1=23. The frozen absolute-fit rule is pM=P(χ232≥χM2)≥0.01. \\boxed{p_M=P(\\chi^2_{23}\\ge\\chi_M^2)\\ge0.01.} The 0.010.01 level is a protocol-control false-rejection guard, not a physical constant. 6. Relative model preference For k=1k=1 fitted parameter and n=24n=24, AICcM=2ℒM+2k+2k(k+1)n−k−1. \\mathrm{AICc}_M= 2\\mathcal L_M+2k+ \\frac{2k(k+1)}{n-k-1}. Define ΔAICc=AICcP−AICcH. \\boxed{\\Delta\\mathrm{AICc}=\\mathrm{AICc}_P-\\mathrm{AICc}_H.} Frozen strong-preference threshold: |ΔAICc|≥10. \\boxed{|\\Delta\\mathrm{AICc}|\\ge10.} Positive values favor HCB1; negative values favor PLB1. 7. Verdicts HCB1_PASS_EMPIRICAL_SCOPED Require pH≥0.01,ΔAICc≥10. p_H\\ge0.01, \\qquad \\Delta\\mathrm{AICc}\\ge10. PLB1_PASS_EMPIRICAL_SCOPED Require pP≥0.01,ΔAICc≤−10. p_P\\ge0.01, \\qquad \\Delta\\mathrm{AICc}\\le-10. NEITHER_SIMPLE_BRIDGE If pP<0.01andpH<0.01. p_P<0.01 \\quad\\text{and}\\quad p_H<0.01. EMPIRICAL_INDETERMINATE All remaining source-complete cases, including weak relative preference, both models fitting adequately, or one model failing without strong evidence for the other. No coefficient retuning, intercept insertion, extra-scatter fit, event deletion or threshold repair is allowed after endpoint exposure. 8. Diagnostics The scorer additionally reports: weighted class means of ε\\varepsilon and Λ\\Lambda; empirical class burden ratio RB=ε‾1/ε‾0R_B=\\bar\\varepsilon_1/\\bar\\varepsilon_0 when defined; leakage class ratio RΛR_\\Lambda; leakage-stationarity z statistic; exact v0.1-equivalent residuals evaluated on weighted class means; standardized residuals per run. These diagnostics do not change the frozen verdict logic. 9. Uncertainty-completeness gate The laboratory’s reported standard uncertainties must already include all declared calibration, acquisition, integration and repeatability contributions selected in the pre-unblind uncertainty protocol. The scorer will not infer an extra noise term from the observed residuals. If the uncertainty model is known incomplete, status is NO_SCORE_UNCERTAINTY_MODEL_INCOMPLETE. 10. Scope A pass establishes only empirical compatibility/preference for the declared operational burden/leakage observables on the implemented bench. It does not establish particle identity, universal EBE_B, fundamental matter burden or physical unification. PHYSICAL PROMOTION=0. \\boxed{\\text{PHYSICAL PROMOTION}=0.}"
